{"content_hash": "ff219a284a839bc9", "version_id": 465, "article_id": 47, "level_code": "en_c1", "lang": "en", "level": 5, "level_label": "C1 高级", "title": "Flock cuts 270 jobs as AI camera backlash grows", "title_zh": "AI摄像头争议升温，Flock裁员270人", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "guardian_tech", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/09/flock-job-cuts", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1562739974-e15519c03d87?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8OHx8c3VydmVpbGxhbmNlJTIwc3RhcnR1cCUyMGZsb2NrfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE2NjU4NTR8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Kaspars Eglitis on Unsplash", "author": "Kaspars Eglitis", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@kasparseglitis?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/bird-on-white-cctv-camera-BCMCMuTISio?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(321, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(359, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "9651cefffeca"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-09", "word_count": 269, "reading_minutes": 1.3, "lead": "Flock Safety, the Atlanta-based maker of AI-powered license-plate readers, is shedding roughly 18% of its workforce after a voluntary buyout fell short, as privacy protests and regulatory pushback mount.", "lead_zh": "总部位于亚特兰大的AI车牌识别摄像头制造商Flock Safety将裁减约18%的员工，此前自愿离职计划未能达到预期，同时隐私抗议和监管阻力不断加剧。", "preview": "Flock Safety intends to eliminate about 270 positions, or roughly 18% of its staff, according to people with direct knowledge of the plans. ", "preview_zh": "据直接了解该计划的人士透露，Flock Safety打算裁减约270个职位，约占其员工总数的18%。此次裁员是在9月宣布的自愿买断计划之后进行的，将于本月底生效。该公司约有1500名员工，拒绝置评；消息人士因该计划尚未公开而要求匿名。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 452, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/47/en_c1.mp3", "duration": 127.05, "size_bytes": 766080, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 313, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/465.json", "paragraphs": ["Flock Safety intends to eliminate about 270 positions, or roughly 18% of its staff, according to people with direct knowledge of the plans. The cuts, which follow a voluntary buyout program announced in September, will take effect at the end of the month. The company, which employs about 1,500 people, declined to comment, and sources spoke on condition of anonymity because the plan has not been made public.", "The layoffs underscore the mounting scrutiny facing the surveillance startup. Its network of some 120,000 AI-powered cameras, affixed to streets and highways across 49 states, automatically reads license plates and records passing vehicles. A recent Reuters/Ipsos poll found Americans divided: 38% support Flock cameras in their communities, while 47% oppose them.", "Public backlash has intensified. In September, Florida banned automated license plate readers from state highways, citing privacy risks tied to Flock’s technology. Home Depot investors have demanded reviews of the retailer’s partnerships with surveillance vendors after reports that Flock’s data was used in immigration enforcement. The company also faces a privacy lawsuit in Virginia alleging warrantless surveillance.", "Despite the controversy, Flock has attracted strong venture capital interest. Founded in 2017 and based in Atlanta, it has raised more than $950m, including a $275m round in March led by Andreessen Horowitz that valued it at $7.5bn. The funds have supported a new US manufacturing facility and an upcoming push into drones. Flock supplies cameras and software to over 4,800 law enforcement agencies and nearly 1,000 businesses.", "Alongside AI datacenters, Flock’s cameras have become a flashpoint ahead of November’s midterm elections, with candidates increasingly attacking opponents by tying them to the technology."], "paragraphs_zh": ["据直接了解该计划的人士透露，Flock Safety打算裁减约270个职位，约占其员工总数的18%。此次裁员是在9月宣布的自愿买断计划之后进行的，将于本月底生效。该公司约有1500名员工，拒绝置评；消息人士因该计划尚未公开而要求匿名。", "此次裁员凸显了这家监控初创公司面临的日益严格的审查。其约12万台AI摄像头网络遍布49个州的街道和高速公路，自动读取车牌并记录过往车辆。路透社/益普索最近的一项民调显示，美国民众意见分歧：38%的人支持在社区使用Flock摄像头，而47%的人反对。", "公众的反对声浪愈演愈烈。9月，佛罗里达州以Flock技术带来的隐私风险为由，禁止在该州高速公路上使用自动车牌识别器。家得宝的投资者要求审查该零售商与监控供应商的合作关系，此前有报道称Flock的数据被用于移民执法。该公司还在弗吉尼亚州面临一起隐私诉讼，指控其无证监控。", "尽管存在争议，Flock仍吸引了强烈的风险投资兴趣。该公司成立于2017年，总部位于亚特兰大，已筹集超过9.5亿美元，其中包括3月由安德森·霍洛维茨领投的2.75亿美元融资，使其估值达到75亿美元。这些资金支持了新的美国制造工厂以及即将推出的无人机产品。Flock向4800多个执法机构和近1000家企业提供摄像头和软件。", "与AI数据中心一样，Flock的摄像头已成为11月中期选举前的一个引爆点，候选人越来越多地通过将对手与该技术挂钩来攻击对方。"], "body": "Flock Safety intends to eliminate about 270 positions, or roughly 18% of its staff, according to people with direct knowledge of the plans. The cuts, which follow a voluntary buyout program announced in September, will take effect at the end of the month. The company, which employs about 1,500 people, declined to comment, and sources spoke on condition of anonymity because the plan has not been made public.\n\nThe layoffs underscore the mounting scrutiny facing the surveillance startup. Its network of some 120,000 AI-powered cameras, affixed to streets and highways across 49 states, automatically reads license plates and records passing vehicles. A recent Reuters/Ipsos poll found Americans divided: 38% support Flock cameras in their communities, while 47% oppose them.\n\nPublic backlash has intensified. In September, Florida banned automated license plate readers from state highways, citing privacy risks tied to Flock’s technology. Home Depot investors have demanded reviews of the retailer’s partnerships with surveillance vendors after reports that Flock’s data was used in immigration enforcement. The company also faces a privacy lawsuit in Virginia alleging warrantless surveillance.\n\nDespite the controversy, Flock has attracted strong venture capital interest. Founded in 2017 and based in Atlanta, it has raised more than $950m, including a $275m round in March led by Andreessen Horowitz that valued it at $7.5bn. The funds have supported a new US manufacturing facility and an upcoming push into drones. Flock supplies cameras and software to over 4,800 law enforcement agencies and nearly 1,000 businesses.\n\nAlongside AI datacenters, Flock’s cameras have become a flashpoint ahead of November’s midterm elections, with candidates increasingly attacking opponents by tying them to the technology.", "body_zh": "据直接了解该计划的人士透露，Flock Safety打算裁减约270个职位，约占其员工总数的18%。此次裁员是在9月宣布的自愿买断计划之后进行的，将于本月底生效。该公司约有1500名员工，拒绝置评；消息人士因该计划尚未公开而要求匿名。\n\n此次裁员凸显了这家监控初创公司面临的日益严格的审查。其约12万台AI摄像头网络遍布49个州的街道和高速公路，自动读取车牌并记录过往车辆。路透社/益普索最近的一项民调显示，美国民众意见分歧：38%的人支持在社区使用Flock摄像头，而47%的人反对。\n\n公众的反对声浪愈演愈烈。9月，佛罗里达州以Flock技术带来的隐私风险为由，禁止在该州高速公路上使用自动车牌识别器。家得宝的投资者要求审查该零售商与监控供应商的合作关系，此前有报道称Flock的数据被用于移民执法。该公司还在弗吉尼亚州面临一起隐私诉讼，指控其无证监控。\n\n尽管存在争议，Flock仍吸引了强烈的风险投资兴趣。该公司成立于2017年，总部位于亚特兰大，已筹集超过9.5亿美元，其中包括3月由安德森·霍洛维茨领投的2.75亿美元融资，使其估值达到75亿美元。这些资金支持了新的美国制造工厂以及即将推出的无人机产品。Flock向4800多个执法机构和近1000家企业提供摄像头和软件。\n\n与AI数据中心一样，Flock的摄像头已成为11月中期选举前的一个引爆点，候选人越来越多地通过将对手与该技术挂钩来攻击对方。", "text": "Flock Safety intends to eliminate about 270 positions, or roughly 18% of its staff, according to people with direct knowledge of the plans. The cuts, which follow a voluntary buyout program announced in September, will take effect at the end of the month. The company, which employs about 1,500 people, declined to comment, and sources spoke on condition of anonymity because the plan has not been made public. The layoffs underscore the mounting scrutiny facing the surveillance startup. Its network of some 120,000 AI-powered cameras, affixed to streets and highways across 49 states, automatically reads license plates and records passing vehicles. A recent Reuters/Ipsos poll found Americans divided: 38% support Flock cameras in their communities, while 47% oppose them. Public backlash has intensified. In September, Florida banned automated license plate readers from state highways, citing privacy risks tied to Flock’s technology. Home Depot investors have demanded reviews of the retailer’s partnerships with surveillance vendors after reports that Flock’s data was used in immigration enforcement. The company also faces a privacy lawsuit in Virginia alleging warrantless surveillance. Despite the controversy, Flock has attracted strong venture capital interest. Founded in 2017 and based in Atlanta, it has raised more than $950m, including a $275m round in March led by Andreessen Horowitz that valued it at $7.5bn. The funds have supported a new US manufacturing facility and an upcoming push into drones. Flock supplies cameras and software to over 4,800 law enforcement agencies and nearly 1,000 businesses. Alongside AI datacenters, Flock’s cameras have become a flashpoint ahead of November’s midterm elections, with candidates increasingly attacking opponents by tying them to the technology.", "vocab": [{"word": "shed", "pos": "verb", "zh": "裁减（员工）；去除", "note": "常用于裁员语境，如 shed jobs/employees", "phonetic": "ʃed", "en": "an outbuilding with a single story; used for shelter or storage"}, {"word": "backlash", "pos": "noun", "zh": "强烈反对；抵制", "note": "常与 against 搭配，指公众的激烈反应", "phonetic": "'bæklæʃ", "en": "an adverse reaction to some political or social occurrence"}, {"word": "scrutiny", "pos": "noun", "zh": "审查；仔细检查", "note": "常用 under scrutiny 表示受到审查", "phonetic": "'skru:tini", "en": "a prolonged intense look"}, {"word": "buyout", "pos": "noun", "zh": "买断（自愿离职补偿）", "note": "voluntary buyout 指自愿买断计划", "phonetic": "ˈbaɪaʊt", "en": "acquisition of a company by purchasing a controlling percentage of its stock"}, {"word": "anonymity", "pos": "noun", "zh": "匿名", "note": "on condition of anonymity 表示匿名条件下", "phonetic": ".ænә'nimiti", "en": "the state of being anonymous"}, {"word": "affix", "pos": "verb", "zh": "固定；附上", "note": "此处指摄像头安装在街道上", "phonetic": "ә'fiks", "en": "a linguistic element added to a word to produce an inflected or derived form"}, {"word": "intensify", "pos": "verb", "zh": "加剧；强化", "note": "常与 backlash、pressure 等搭配", "phonetic": "in'tensifai", "en": "make more intense, stronger, or more marked"}, {"word": "warrantless", "pos": "adj", "zh": "无搜查令的", "note": "法律语境，指未经授权", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "flashpoint", "pos": "noun", "zh": "引爆点；冲突焦点", "note": "指争议或冲突的触发点", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "venture capital", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "风险投资", "note": "常缩写为 VC", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "valuation", "pos": "noun", "zh": "估值", "note": "动词为 value，指公司价值", "phonetic": ".vælju'eiʃәn", "en": "assessed price"}, {"word": "deployment", "pos": "noun", "zh": "部署；应用", "note": "常指技术或设备的广泛使用", "phonetic": "", "en": "the distribution of forces in preparation for battle or work"}, {"word": "alleged", "pos": "adj", "zh": "涉嫌的；据称的", "note": "用于法律或新闻报道中表示未经证实", "phonetic": "ә'ledʒd", "en": "declared but not proved"}, {"word": "midterm elections", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "中期选举", "note": "美国每两年一次，在总统任期中举行", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "AI surveillance startup Flock to cut several hundred jobs amid backlash, sources say", "summary_original": "Company, which grown rapidly in recent years, has been under scrutiny as privacy concerns grow\nFlock Safety plans to shed about 18% of its employees, people with direct ⁠knowledge of the plans said on Thursday, as the maker of\nAI\n-powered\nsurveillance\ncameras and license-plate readers faces\nmounting opposition\nto its products from communities and ⁠lawmakers.\nThe people said the job ⁠cuts came after ​a voluntary buyout program and were expected to affect roughly 270 employees at Flock, a surveillance technology startup that has seen rapid growth in recent ⁠years. Employees will leave the company at the end of the month.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "AI surveillance startup Flock to cut several hundred jobs amid backlash, sources say\nCompany, which grown rapidly in recent years, has been under scrutiny as privacy concerns grow\nFlock Safety plans to shed about 18% of its employees, people with direct ⁠knowledge of the plans said on Thursday, as the maker of\nAI\n-powered\nsurveillance\ncameras and license-plate readers faces\nmounting opposition\nto its products from communities and ⁠lawmakers.\nThe people said the job ⁠cuts came after ​a voluntary buyout program and were expected to affect roughly 270 employees at Flock, a surveillance technology startup that has seen rapid growth in recent ⁠years. Employees will leave the company at the end of the month.\nSources declined to be identified as the company has yet to make the plan public.\nFlock declined ⁠to comment.\nIn September, Flock announced a voluntary separation program, asking employees to apply if they wanted to ​leave the company, as Wired reported. The ‌company has about 1,500 employees.\nFlock faces ‌\ngrowing scrutiny\nfrom regulators, lawmakers and privacy advocates, despite drawing strong investor interest among venture capitalists. A ‌recent Reuters/Ipsos poll showed Americans are divided on whether Flock cameras are a good idea. About 38% of the country supports the use of Flock cameras in their community, compared with 47% who oppose their use.\nAcross 49 states, Flock’s network of about 120,000 AI-powered cameras, affixed to streets and highways, automatically read license plates and record vehicles as they pass.\nThe company, based in Atlanta and founded in ‌2017, has raised more than $950m from venture capital investors, with its latest $275m round in March led by Andreessen Horowitz valuing the company at $7.5bn. The funds have supported a ​new US manufacturing facility and an upcoming push into drone products, according to the company.\nFlock provides cameras and software to more than 4,800 law enforcement agencies and nearly 1,000 businesses. The company says its technology helps investigate and solve crimes, but it has come under increasing scrutiny over alleged privacy violations and data-sharing practices.\nPublic backlash ⁠has grown. In September, Florida banned automated license plate readers from state highways, ​citing privacy risks tied to Flock’s ​cameras.\nHome Depot investors recently demanded reviews ​of the retailer’s partnerships with surveillance technology vendors after reports that Flock’s data was used ​in immigration enforcement.\nFlock also ‌faces legal challenges, such ​as a privacy ​lawsuit in Virginia alleging that the widespread deployment of its AI-powered cameras constitutes warrantless surveillance.\nTogether with AI datacenters, Flock cameras have emerged as a flashpoint ahead of November’s midterm elections, with candidates increasingly attacking their opponents by tying them to the technology.\nExplore more on these topics\nSurveillance\nAI (artificial intelligence)\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T20:57:32.679444", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Flock", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.488, "sm": 100, "em": 487, "cs": 0, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Safety", "s": 0.5, "e": 0.912, "sm": 500, "em": 912, "cs": 6, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "intends", "s": 0.925, "e": 1.388, "sm": 925, "em": 1387, "cs": 13, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "to", "s": 1.4, "e": 1.512, "sm": 1400, "em": 1512, "cs": 21, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "eliminate", "s": 1.525, "e": 2.075, "sm": 1525, "em": 2075, "cs": 24, "ce": 33, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "about", "s": 2.087, "e": 2.362, "sm": 2087, "em": 2362, "cs": 34, "ce": 39, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "270", "s": 2.375, "e": 3.312, "sm": 2375, "em": 3312, "cs": 40, "ce": 43, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "positions", "s": 3.325, "e": 3.963, "sm": 3325, "em": 3962, "cs": 44, "ce": 53, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": ",", "s": 3.963, "e": 4.3, "sm": 3962, "em": 4300, "cs": 53, "ce": 54, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "or", "s": 4.3, "e": 4.5, "sm": 4300, "em": 4500, "cs": 55, "ce": 57, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "roughly", "s": 4.513, "e": 4.95, "sm": 4512, "em": 4950, "cs": 58, "ce": 65, "si": 0}, {"i": 1